tasklist

Lists all currently running processes on the system, including system and user applications.


tasklist /svc: Displays the services hosted in each process.

tasklist /fi "memusage gt 50000": Filters processes consuming more than 50 MB of memory.

tasklist /fi "imagename eq notepad.exe": Displays only processes with a specific name.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

taskkill

Terminates a running process by name or Process ID (PID).

taskkill /im <processname> [/f] [/t] Parameters: /im <processname> – Specifies the process name (e.g., notepad.exe)  /f – Forces termination of the process  /t – Terminates the process and any child proce


taskkill /pid 4321 /f: Terminate a process using its PID.

taskkill /im chrome.exe /t /f: Terminate Google Chrome and all its child processes forcefully.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

driverquery

Displays a list of all installed device drivers along with detailed information about each driver.

driverquery /v /fo <format> Parameters: /v – Displays detailed (verbose) information about each driver  /fo <format> – Specifies the output format: TABLE, LIST, or CSV

driverquery /v: displays detailed information including memory usage and module type.

driverquery /fo csv: outputs driver information in CSV format for easy import into spreadsheets. driverquery /fo list: outputs each driver’s information in a readable list format.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wmic

Accesses Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) to retrieve detailed system information, including OS, hardware, and configuration data.

wmic os get <property>

Common Properties: 
Caption – Displays the operating system name  
Version – Displays the OS version 
LastBootUpTime – Displays the last system boot time
FreePhysicalMemory – Displays available RAM

wmic os get version:displays the Windows version.

wmic os get lastbootuptime:Shows when the system was last restarted.

wmic cpu get name:Displays the processor name.

wmic memorychip get capacity:Displays installed RAM modules and their sizes.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

chkdsk

Checks a disk for errors and displays a status report.

chkdsk <drive>: [/f] [/r] Parameters: <drive>: – Specifies the drive letter to check (e.g., C:)  /f – Fixes errors found on the disk  /r – Locates bad sectors and recovers readable information

chkdsk C: /f: Checks the drive and fixes errors automatically.

chkdsk C: /r: Checks the drive for bad sectors and recovers readable data.

chkdsk D: /f /r: Performs a full scan with fixes on a different drive (D: in this example).

